# Test Quality Standards

RULE: Expand existing test files; never create test_*_extended.py, test_*_additional.py, test_*_v2.py. Use singleton fixtures from conftest; mock external deps.
WHY: Duplicate files and fixtures cause maintenance burden; real GCS/API in unit tests slows gates.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/testing.md

DO: Add tests to existing test_config.py; create new file only for uncovered module; use session/module scope fixtures; mock GCS, APIs, get_secret_client
NEVER: Create test_config_extended.py, test_adapter_2.py; duplicate fixtures; use real GCS in unit tests; 500MB fixtures

## Mocking (essential)

Unit tests never make real network calls. Use autouse conftest fixtures. For get_secret_client: patch with _UNIT_TEST_SECRETS dict; raise SecretNotFoundError if unregistered. For get_storage_client: MagicMock(spec=StorageClient). Libraries that DEFINE get_secret_client: mock SecretManagerClient instead.
Full pattern: CODEX 06-coding-standards/testing.md#mocking-get_secret_client-in-unit-tests-canonical-pattern
